+                    // PATCH 0001: publish the flight `connect()` just produced.
+                    //
+                    // `connect()` queues the ClientHello as a transmit, but this
+                    // pipeline only drains `poll_transmit()` in `handle_timeout`.
+                    // A caller that advances time on `poll_timeout()` alone,
+                    // which is the correct sans-I/O contract, then waits for the
+                    // next scheduled timer before the ClientHello leaves. During
+                    // ICE establishment that timer can be the ICE check
+                    // interval, so the handshake stalls for up to that interval.
+                    // Draining here attaches the output to the event that caused
+                    // it, with no timer and no artificial timeout pass.
+                    while let Some(transmit) = dtls_endpoint.poll_transmit() {
